pe": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rollback to v2.3.0 blocked", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api is failing health checks on v2.3.1 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), error rate 0.18. Per the runbook I tried to roll back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy). The rollback call returned 503 Service Unavailable twice; service status confirms it is still on v2.3.1 in all regions. No changes were applied. Needs manual rollback to v2.3.0 or investigation of the rollback service outage.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I could not roll checkout-api back. The rollback to v2.3.0 failed twice with `503 Service Unavailable`, and checkout-api is still on v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of 0.18.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy, and v2.3.0 has a healthy production record, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Rollback:** Two attempts, both 503. A status check between them showed no partial change.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api, which paged on-call. It describes the failing v2.3.1 deploy, the blocked rollback to v2.3.0, and that nothing was changed.\n\nSomeone will need to retry the rollback to v2.3.0 once the rollback service is available again, or roll back manually if the outage persists. I did not make a third attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}